
## PROBLEM STATEMENT ##

Given the root of a binary tree, return an array of the largest value in each row of the tree (0-indexed).
Example 1:
Input: root = [1,3,2,5,3,null,9]
Output: [1,3,9]
Example 2:
Input: root = [1,2,3]
Output: [1,3]
Constraints:
The number of nodes in the tree will be in the range [0, 104].
-231 <= Node.val <= 231 - 1

## SOLUTION ##

class Solution:
    def largestValues(self, root: Optional[TreeNode]) -> List[int]:
        res = []

        if not root:
            return res
        
        q = deque()
        q.append(root)

        while q:
            max_val = float("-inf")
            for _ in range(len(q)):
                node = q.popleft()
                max_val = max(max_val, node.val)

                if node.left:
                    q.append(node.left)

                if node.right:
                    q.append(node.right)                    

            res.append(max_val)

        return res
